# <%= current_page.data.title %>

This section explains the common delivery workflow used at HMCTS.

Use the guidance in this order so teams follow one consistent setup path from a new repository to production:

1. For application services, start with runtime guidance in [Starting a new component](../new-component/) (Java, Node.js, Python)
2. [Create a new GitHub repository](../new-component/github-repo.html)
3. [Add the repository to Jenkins](../new-component/jenkins-repository.html)
4. [Add a Helm chart](../new-component/helm-chart.html) for deployable services
5. [Add infrastructure as code](../new-component/infrastructure-as-code.html) where infrastructure is required
6. [Configure GitOps with Flux](../new-component/gitops-flux.html#application-config-in-flux)
7. [Set up secrets management](../new-component/secrets-management.html)
8. [Configure load balancer](../new-component/load-balancer-configuration.html) for backend services
9. [Configure TLS certificates](../new-component/tls-certificates.html)
10. [Configure Public DNS](../new-component/public-dns.html)
11. [Configure Front Door](../new-component/front-door.html) for frontend services
12. [Use feature flags](../new-component/feature-flags.html) to decouple deployment from release

